the family of a man killed in a  suspected DUI crash last month is  speaking out tonight police say that  Lenny corello was hit and killed near  Gowen and Decatur and that the other  driver involved was under the influence  and speeding Sasha Loftus joins us now  with the story you'll only see on eight  news now  [Music]  listen away from his house  driver and died on impact her family  understandably is devastated and she  wants to see more done to prevent more  crashes like this he loved everybody he  loved life Felicity Carter remembers  what she loved about her uncle Lenny  carella those memories like all of us  are so grateful that we had those last  happy moments the 71 year old suddenly  lost his life in September when police  say he was hit by an impaired driver  down the street from his home near  Decatur and Gowen this didn't just  impact one person this impact several  lives  so far this year 45 people have been  killed in DUI crashes in metro police  jurisdiction we need director penalties  for driving Under the Influence retired  Nevada State Police Captain Scott Martin  believes a solution starts with stricter  penalties for first-time offenders he  also says enforcement is key to catch  those under the influence before someone  gets hurt what it comes down to is the  lack of resources and the lack of police  officers that are out on the road  Felicity tells me her family isn't just  grieving they're also angry if you're  caught drinking and driving there needs  to be bigger consequences and she hopes  sharing Lenny's story will help others  understand what it means when the worst  happens it makes you wonder why the good  ones are always taken first felicity's  family has started a GoFundMe to help  with Lenny's funeral expenses now the  man accused of hitting him 20-year-old  Corey Clark was arrested on a felony  charge of reckless driving resulting in  death and substantial bodily harm Sasha  Loftus 8 News Now
 

